{"id":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","turns":[{"turn":1,"said":"What shutter speed should I use at 25 frames a second?","kind":"question","expected":"Any answer; nothing changes","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"For 25 frames per second, use **1/50 second**.\n\nThis follows the 180° shutter rule (1/(2 × frame rate)), which gives natural motion blur. Your camera is already set to 1/50 at 25p, so you're good to go.","calls":[],"decisionMs":1190.1259170000012,"totalMs":1190.1457500000015,"steps":1,"generatedTokens":66,"timedOut":false},{"turn":2,"said":"Set the aperture to f/5.6.","kind":"request","expected":"Aperture f/5.6; ISO and shutter unchanged","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Aperture is now set to f/5.6. This will make the image a bit darker and increase your depth of field.","calls":[{"name":"set_setting","arguments":{"setting":"aperture","value":"f/5.6"},"valid":true,"changesSomething":true}],"decisionMs":968.7291249999998,"totalMs":1379.7342499999995,"steps":2,"generatedTokens":70,"timedOut":false},{"turn":3,"said":"Is my exposure okay?","kind":"question","expected":"Any answer; nothing changes","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"Your exposure looks good. The histogram shows a mean brightness of 33%, with no clipped highlights or crushed shadows. You have about 2 stops of highlight headroom, which is safe. The waveform is fairly even across the frame. No adjustments needed unless you want it brighter.","calls":[{"name":"analyze_frame","arguments":{},"valid":true,"changesSomething":false}],"decisionMs":1697.3618749999987,"totalMs":1697.368124999999,"steps":2,"generatedTokens":73,"timedOut":false},{"turn":4,"said":"Make it a bit brighter.","kind":"request","expected":"A bit brighter; shutter stays","passed":true,"failures":[],"credit":1,"reply":"ISO raised to 1250, making the image a bit brighter as requested.","calls":[{"name":"adjust_exposure","arguments":{"stops":0.5,"using":"auto"},"valid":true,"changesSomething":true}],"deci